      "successfulRequestCount": 1,
      "loggedRequestAttempts": 1,
      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 134,
      "outputTokens": 979,
      "costUsd": 0.008877999999999999,
      "pronunciationText": "The same thing happens in any arithmetic sequence. Write the sum forwards, from the first term, a, up to the last term, a sub n. Then write the same sum backwards underneath. In each column, the top term goes up by d and the bottom term goes down by d, so every column adds to a plus a sub n. There are n columns, so two lots of S sub n is n times ay plus a sub n. Halve it, and S sub n is n over two, times ay plus a sub n. In words, it's the average of the first and last terms, times how many terms there are."
    },
