      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 122,
      "outputTokens": 783,
      "costUsd": 0.007108000000000001,
      "pronunciationText": "Find the sum of the first twenty terms of three, seven, eleven, and so on. Here ay is three, d is four, and n is twenty. We don't know the last term, so use the second form. That's ten, times six plus nineteen fours. Nineteen fours is seventy-six, so it's ten times eighty-two, which is eight hundred and twenty. Check with the first form. The twentieth term is three plus seventy-six, which is seventy-nine, and ten times three plus seventy-nine is also eight hundred and twenty."
    },
