      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 128,
      "outputTokens": 819,
      "costUsd": 0.007435,
      "pronunciationText": "Now, the sum of all the whole numbers from fifty to two hundred. It's arithmetic, with d equal to one. The first term is fifty, and the last is two hundred, so the first form fits. But how many terms are there? Not one hundred and fifty. It's two hundred minus fifty, plus one, which is one hundred and fifty-one. So the sum is one hundred and fifty-one over two, times fifty plus two hundred. That's one hundred and fifty-one, times one hundred and twenty-five, which is eighteen thousand, eight hundred and seventy-five."
