      "outputTokens": 978,
      "costUsd": 0.0088695,
      "pronunciationText": "Here's a surprise. How many terms of eleven, plus nine, plus seven, and so on, add up to thirty-two? Here ay is eleven and d is minus two, so S sub n simplifies to n times twelve minus n. Set that equal to thirty-two, and the quadratic has two roots: four and eight. Both are whole numbers, and both work. Four terms make thirty-two. The next four terms are three, one, minus one and minus three, and they add to zero, so eight terms make thirty-two again. When the terms go negative, the sum can come back down, so check every root."
