      "costUsd": 0.004751999999999999,
      "pronunciationText": "Here's the short version. An arithmetic sum is the average of the first and last terms, times how many terms there are. It's guaranteed for arithmetic sequences, because their terms always pair up evenly. Other lists might not. For one, plus two, plus four, it gives seven and a half, but the real sum is seven."
