      "pronunciationText": "Here ay is five, d is three and n is thirty. The thirtieth term is five plus twenty-nine threes, which is ninety-two. So the sum is fifteen, times five plus ninety-two, which is one thousand four hundred and fifty-five. Fifteen hundred is wrong. It uses thirty steps of three, instead of twenty-nine."
