      "pronunciationText": "Here ay is two and d is four, so S sub n simplifies to two n squared. Two n squared is more than two hundred when n squared is more than a hundred, so n is more than ten. Ten terms make exactly two hundred, which isn't more. So the answer is eleven terms. Ten is wrong. It reaches two hundred, but doesn't go over."
